From: Guohan Lu <securely1g@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve base users and groups when adding service accounts

Add accounts(base, architecture, users, groups) alongside passwd and group.
Read the base OCI layers, retain inherited records, reject conflicting names
and IDs, then reuse the existing account writers and TAR toolchain. Existing
passwd/group behavior remains unchanged. A declared Python execution toolchain
and BSD tar handle plain, gzip, xz and zstd account layers.

Origin: SONiC's source-built base and Syncd images need Redis and _ssh additions
without copying a stale Debian account list. This is the rules_distroless
implementation submitted in https://github.com/bazel-contrib/rules_distroless/pull/290
referencing https://github.com/bazel-contrib/rules_distroless/issues/278.
Backport: Adapt the existing MODULE Python dependency and toolchain registration to the reviewed upstream 0.9.4
plus SONiC .12 locked-import and installer patch stack; generic rule and regression bytes match the
upstream proposal in securely1g/rules_distroless commit
d503c1141d3759390dc78ffbb99de33b7d4f4619 (codex/preserve-base-accounts).
Retain this local patch until an upstream release containing the feature is
selected and the original tests pass on native AMD64 and ARM64.

Signed-off-by: Guohan Lu <securely1g@gmail.com>

